.vercel
.env*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
web/.next/
.superpowers/
.venv/
mplads-data/
docs/deck/references/

# graphify: the graph and its report are worth sharing, the AST cache is not -
# it is rebuilt from source and is per-version.
graphify-out/cache/
# Per-developer permission grants, not a project decision.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Installed agent skills. The lockfile beside this records what to install
# (`npx skills experimental_install`); the skills themselves are a local tool,
# and /brag alone ships 17 MB of bundled music.
.claude/skills/

# The /brag video's borrowed assets: bundled music whose licence has not been
# verified for redistribution, CC0 sound effects, font files copied out of the
# Next build, and a vendored GSAP. All restorable - see the README beside them.
brag-output/composition/assets/*
!brag-output/composition/assets/README.md
video-explainer/composition/assets/*
!video-explainer/composition/assets/README.md
# The generated narration: ~14 MB of wav, regenerated by the tts command in
# video-explainer/README.md. The scripts beside them are the source of truth.
video-explainer/vo/*.wav
video-explainer/vo/durations.json

# The deck's diagram renderer is a node package; its node_modules is not ours
# to commit. `npm install` in docs/deck/diagrams restores it.
docs/deck/diagrams/node_modules/
# Generated from boards.template.html at build time.
docs/deck/diagrams/boards.html
# Rebuilt by scripts/preview_deck.py whenever the deck changes.
docs/deck/preview/
